Feature: artie generate: a run's capture, made a script with no model in it
  spec/PLAN-SCRIPT-GENERATOR.md. artie generate reads a run's capture (its
  YAML trace) and writes a script that makes every selection the run made,
  nested as it nested, with no reason step: each value is an input, a member
  read again from the answer of the step that brought it into the run, or a
  constant. A value the reasoner chose, which the words don't give, is frozen
  as the constant it was and marked for review. Beside the script, a lock file
  pins what the run was offered: the rung, each form's integrity and the sets
  it was offered in, each link's target. The same capture always gives the
  same script.

  Background:
    Given a service holds these resources
      | address    | title                 | state |
      | /          | Repositories          |       |
      | /issues/10 | Login fails on Safari |       |
      | /c/502     | Seen in #10.          |       |
    And these forms
      | at         | relation   | leads to   | outcome      |
      | /          | open-issue | /issues/10 | new resource |
      | /          | issues-get | /issues/10 | done         |
      | /issues/10 | comment    | /c/502     | new resource |
      | /issues/10 | close      | /issues/10 | done         |
    And the resource at "/issues/10" holds
      """
      {"number": 10, "title": "Login fails on Safari"}
      """
    And the form "issues-get" at "/" asks for these fields, typed
      | field  | type    |
      | number | integer |

  Scenario: A reasoned run becomes a script with no reason step, which makes the same selections
    Given the script "close.kts" is
      """kotlin
      val title by input()

      heart("scripted://service/") {
          var issue = 0L
          act(intent = "open an issue titled $title") {
              issue = state.long("number")
          }
          act(intent = "open issue $issue") {
              act(intent = "comment on it: Seen in #$issue.") {}
              act(intent = "close it, since it's done")
          }
      }
      """
    And the reasoner chooses
      | intent                                     | selection | relation   | fields                    |
      | open an issue titled Login fails on Safari | act       | open-issue | {"title": "Login fails on Safari"} |
      | open issue 10                              | act       | issues-get | {"number": "10"}          |
      | comment on it: Seen in #10.                | act       | comment    | {"body": "Seen in #10."}  |
      | close it, since it's done                  | act       | close      | {"reason": "completed"}   |
    When artie is run with
      | argument                    |
      | run                         |
      | close.kts                   |
      | title=Login fails on Safari |
      | --reasoner                  |
      | claude                      |
      | --trace                     |
      | run.trace.yaml              |
    Then artie exits 0
    When artie is run with
      | argument       |
      | generate       |
      | run.trace.yaml |
      | --out          |
      | gen.kts        |
      | --script       |
      | close.kts      |
    Then artie exits 0
    And artie prints
      | line                                         |
      | wrote gen.kts: 1 value to review             |
      | wrote gen.pins.yaml: 4 forms and 0 links pinned |
      | wrote gen.derivation.yaml: 5 derivations        |
    And the file "gen.kts" reads
      """kotlin
      // Generated by artie generate from run.trace.yaml, the run of close.kts.
      // Every selection as that run made it, nested as it nested, with no model.
      // What it was offered is pinned in gen.pins.yaml, held to before every act.
      // A line marked "review:" holds a value the reasoner chose: check it before keeping the script.
      //   artie run gen.kts title='Login fails on Safari'
      val title by input()

      heart("scripted://service/") {
          var issue = 0L // step 2's /number

          act("open-issue", "title" to title, intent = "open an issue titled $title") {
              issue = state.long("number")
          }
          act("issues-get", "number" to issue, intent = "open issue $issue") {
              act("comment", "body" to "Seen in #$issue.", intent = "comment on it: Seen in #$issue.") {}
              act(
                  "close",
                  "reason" to "completed", // review: the reasoner chose it, asked "close it, since it's done"
                  intent = "close it, since it's done",
              )
          }
      }
      """
    When artie is run with
      | argument                    |
      | run                         |
      | gen.kts                     |
      | title=Login fails on Safari |
      | --trace                     |
      | gen.trace.yaml              |
    Then artie exits 0
    And the run traced in "gen.trace.yaml" made the same selections as the run traced in "run.trace.yaml"

  Scenario: A scripted step's values are bound as its script wrote them, its call on as many lines as it takes
    A step the script wrote as act(...) is read from its whole call: text it
    wrote literally is a constant, a variable it named keeps its name, and a
    string with $slots puts each back by the name the script gave it.
    Given the script "close.kts" is
      """kotlin
      val title by input()

      heart("scripted://service/") {
          var issue = 0L
          act("open-issue", "title" to title) {
              issue = state.long("number")
          }
          act(
              "issues-get",
              "number" to issue,
          ) {
              act("comment", "body" to "Seen in #$issue.") {}
              act("close", "reason" to "completed")
          }
      }
      """
    When artie is run with
      | argument                    |
      | run                         |
      | close.kts                   |
      | title=Login fails on Safari |
      | --trace                     |
      | run.trace.yaml              |
    Then artie exits 0
    When artie is run with
      | argument       |
      | generate       |
      | run.trace.yaml |
      | --out          |
      | gen.kts        |
      | --script       |
      | close.kts      |
    Then artie exits 0
    And the file "gen.kts" reads
      """kotlin
      // Generated by artie generate from run.trace.yaml, the run of close.kts.
      // Every selection as that run made it, nested as it nested, with no model.
      // What it was offered is pinned in gen.pins.yaml, held to before every act.
      //   artie run gen.kts title='Login fails on Safari'
      val title by input()

      heart("scripted://service/") {
          var issue = 0L // step 2's /number

          act("open-issue", "title" to title) {
              issue = state.long("number")
          }
          act("issues-get", "number" to issue) {
              act("comment", "body" to "Seen in #$issue.") {}
              act("close", "reason" to "completed")
          }
      }
      """

  Scenario: Without the script, inputs, waits and checks come from the capture; the lock file pins what was offered
    A value two answers hold is read from the earlier one, the step that
    brought it into the run, whatever order the capture lists them in.
    Given the file "run.trace.yaml" is
      """
      ---
      run:
        inputs:
          owner:
            value: acme
            given: given
          stamp:
            value: 1018-2200
            given: default
            default: 1018-2200
      ---
      mode: script
      say: enter {entry}
      line: 1
      params:
        entry: http://localhost:8392/
      opens: true
      outcome: done
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: open the repository acme
      line: 2
      within: 1
      params:
        relation: repos-get
        owner: acme
      values:
        owner:
          value: acme
          type: string
          from:
            - input: owner
      reason:
        template: open the repository $owner
        slots:
          owner:
            value: acme
            from:
              - input: owner
      opens: true
      chose:
        kind: form
        relation: repos-get
      guard:
        rung: L2
        form: sha256-repos
      outcome: done
      now:
        state:
          name: rockets
          head_sha: abc123
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: follow its branches
      line: 3
      within: 2
      params:
        relation: branches
      reason:
        template: follow its branches
        slots: {}
      chose:
        kind: link
        relation: branches
        target: /repos/{owner}/branches
      guard:
        rung: L2
      outcome: done
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: start a branch named fix-1018-2200
      line: 4
      within: 2
      params:
        relation: start-branch
        name: fix-1018-2200
      values:
        name:
          value: fix-1018-2200
          type: string
          from:
            - parts:
                1018-2200:
                  input: stamp
      reason:
        template: start a branch named fix-$stamp
        slots:
          stamp:
            value: 1018-2200
            from:
              - input: stamp
      opens: true
      chose:
        kind: form
        relation: start-branch
      guard:
        rung: L2
        set:
          integrity: sha256-set1
        form: sha256-start
      outcome: new resource
      now:
        state:
          ref: fix-1018-2200
          sha: abc123
      ---
      mode: script
      say: until
      line: 5
      within: 4
      params: {}
      waited:
        for: offers("merge")
        reads: 2
      outcome: held
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: merge it
      line: 6
      within: 4
      params:
        relation: merge
        sha: abc123
        merge_method: squash
      values:
        sha:
          value: abc123
          type: string
          from:
            - step: 4
              pointer: /sha
            - step: 2
              pointer: /head_sha
        merge_method:
          value: squash
          type: string
          from:
            - chosen
      reason:
        template: merge it
        slots: {}
      chose:
        kind: form
        relation: merge
      guard:
        rung: L2
        set:
          integrity: sha256-set2
        form: sha256-merge
      outcome: done
      ---
      mode: script
      say: check
      line: 7
      within: 4
      params:
        facts:
          - member: merged
            test: eq true
            held: 'true'
            holds: true
      outcome: held
      ---
      mode: script
      say: return to {address}
      line: 4
      within: 2
      params:
        address: http://localhost:8392/repos/acme/branches
      outcome: done
      ---
      mode: script
      say: return to {address}
      line: 2
      within: 1
      params:
        address: http://localhost:8392/
      outcome: done
      """
    When artie is run with
      | argument       |
      | generate       |
      | run.trace.yaml |
      | --out          |
      | gen.kts        |
    Then artie exits 0
    And artie prints
      | line                                         |
      | wrote gen.kts: 1 value to review             |
      | wrote gen.pins.yaml: 3 forms and 1 link pinned |
      | wrote gen.derivation.yaml: 8 derivations       |
    And the file "gen.kts" reads
      """kotlin
      // Generated by artie generate from run.trace.yaml.
      // Every selection as that run made it, nested as it nested, with no model.
      // What it was offered is pinned in gen.pins.yaml, held to before every act.
      // A line marked "review:" holds a value the reasoner chose: check it before keeping the script.
      //   artie run gen.kts owner=acme
      val owner by input()
      val stamp by input(default = "1018-2200")

      heart("http://localhost:8392/") {
          var headSha = "" // step 2's /head_sha

          act("repos-get", "owner" to owner, intent = "open the repository $owner") {
              headSha = state.text("head_sha")
              follow("branches", intent = "follow its branches")
              act("start-branch", "name" to "fix-$stamp", intent = "start a branch named fix-$stamp") {
                  until { offers("merge") }
                  act(
                      "merge",
                      "sha" to headSha,
                      "merge_method" to "squash", // review: the reasoner chose it, asked "merge it"
                      intent = "merge it",
                  )
                  check("merged" eq true)
              }
          }
      }
      """
    And the file "gen.pins.yaml" reads
      """
      # What gen.kts was recorded against, from run.trace.yaml. artie run holds the script to it before every act:
      # --guard lenient (the default) refuses a form no longer offered, or whose integrity changed; --guard strict
      # also refuses one offered in a set not recorded for it.
      rung: L2
      forms:
        repos-get:
          integrity: sha256-repos
          sets: []
        start-branch:
          integrity: sha256-start
          sets:
            - sha256-set1
        merge:
          integrity: sha256-merge
          sets:
            - sha256-set2
      links:
        branches: '{owner}'
      """

  Scenario: A name is put back inside a word, never inside a number; only a selection brings a value in
    Step 2's until re-read the resource: what it read is no source, so the
    sha is written as the constant it was. The slot version's value, 1, is in
    no value as a whole word ("1.2" is a number of its own), so it is never a
    variable.
    Given the file "run.trace.yaml" is
      """
      ---
      run:
        inputs:
          stamp:
            value: 1018-2200
            given: given
      ---
      mode: script
      say: enter {entry}
      line: 1
      params:
        entry: http://localhost:8392/
      opens: true
      outcome: done
      now:
        state:
          version: 1
      ---
      mode: script
      say: until
      line: 2
      within: 1
      params: {}
      waited:
        for: offers("commit-file")
      outcome: held
      now:
        state:
          sha: abc123
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: commit fix-1018-2200.md as 1, saying it was fixed in 1.2
      line: 3
      within: 1
      params:
        relation: commit-file
        path: fix-1018-2200.md
        message: Fixed in 1.2
        sha: abc123
      values:
        path:
          value: fix-1018-2200.md
          from:
            - words
        message:
          value: Fixed in 1.2
          from:
            - paraphrase
        sha:
          value: abc123
          from:
            - step: 2
              pointer: /sha
      reason:
        template: commit fix-$stamp.md as $version, saying it was fixed in 1.2
        slots:
          stamp:
            value: 1018-2200
            from:
              - input: stamp
          version:
            value: '1'
            from:
              - step: 1
                pointer: /version
      chose:
        kind: form
        relation: commit-file
      outcome: done
      """
    When artie is run with
      | argument       |
      | generate       |
      | run.trace.yaml |
      | --out          |
      | gen.kts        |
    Then artie exits 0
    And the file "gen.kts" reads
      """kotlin
      // Generated by artie generate from run.trace.yaml.
      // Every selection as that run made it, nested as it nested, with no model.
      // What it was offered is pinned in gen.pins.yaml, held to before every act.
      //   artie run gen.kts stamp=1018-2200
      val stamp by input()

      heart("http://localhost:8392/") {
          until { offers("commit-file") }
          act(
              "commit-file",
              "path" to "fix-$stamp.md",
              "message" to "Fixed in 1.2",
              "sha" to "abc123",
              intent = "commit fix-$stamp.md as 1, saying it was fixed in 1.2",
          )
      }
      """

  Scenario Outline: Only a run that finished is generated from
    Given the file "run.trace.yaml" is
      """
      ---
      run:
        inputs: {}
      ---
      mode: script
      say: enter {entry}
      line: 1
      params:
        entry: http://localhost:8392/
      outcome: done
      ---
      mode: script
      say: act {relation}
      line: 2
      within: 1
      params:
        relation: close
      outcome: <outcome>
      """
    When artie is run with
      | argument       |
      | generate       |
      | run.trace.yaml |
      | --out          |
      | gen.kts        |
    Then artie exits 2
    And artie's last line is: can't generate from run.trace.yaml: step 2 was <outcome>

    Examples:
      | outcome |
      | refused |
      | failed  |
